  m_Name: Drums
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ExhibitData
  title: Ingoma
  subtitle: 
  story: A drum covered with stretched animal hide and is always wider at the top
    than at the base.  At festive events it's used to welcome guests. The drummers
    play using two wooden sticks called imirishyo . To adjust the instrument's pitch,
    the drumhead is warmed near a small fire or in the sun before playing.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 29fac28b9240f8e4ebd7245c52c1e5a6, type: 3}
  sourceCredit: KMMA/Jos GANSEMANS
